  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed Value near $14.59B (-0.3% 30D) keeps on-chain RWA exposure in a holding pattern\u2014tokenization momentum is still news- and pipeline-driven until distributed value breaks range. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/10/28/securitize-adds-stellar-blockchain-as-institutional-tokenization-gathers-steam\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Securitize adds Stellar blockchain as institutional tokenization gathers steam</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/news/tradfi-and-fintech/ondo-brings-15-stock-tokens-to-robinhood-chain-with-uniswap-pools\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ondo Brings 15 Stock Tokens to Robinhood Chain With Uniswap Pools</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Institutional commitments are still a leading share signal:</strong> Bank and asset-manager distribution deals often shift platform and network leadership before headline RWA totals fully catch up. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/business/2026-10-28-ripple-900-million-revenue-run-rate-rlusd-431920\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ripple expects $900 million annualized product revenue run rate as institutional business expands</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/10/28/brazil-s-largest-lender-becomes-first-bank-to-formalize-crypto-brokerage-under-new-rules\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Brazil\u2019s largest lender becomes first bank to formalize crypto brokerage under new rules</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
